 mp3 file rotation", exc_info=True)\n\ndef main():\n    # Example usage\n    src_directory = \'./mp3_files\'\n    dest_directory = \'./archived_mp3_files\'\n    rotation_days_threshold = 7\n\n    rotate_mp3_files(src_directory, dest_directory, rotation_days_threshold)\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\nThe code execution status:\n{\'success\': False, \'output\': \'\', \'error_message\': \'Traceback (most recent call last):\\n  File "C:\\\\Users\\\\JACK\\\\Desktop\\\\react-node-chatgpt-tutorial\\\\backend\\\\openai-latest.py", line 203, in execute_code\\n    exec(code)\\n  File "<string>", line 58, in <module>\\n  File "<string>", line 55, in main\\nNameError: name \\\'rotate_mp3_files\\\' is not defined\\n\', \'error_output\': \'\'}\nReviewer Advice:The error message you\'re encountering, `NameError: name \'rotate_mp3_files\' is not defined`, suggests that when `main()` is called, it cannot find the reference to the `rotate_mp3_files` function. However, your code correctly defines `rotate_mp3_files` before it is called in the `main` function, which means that the error is likely due to how the code is being executed or referenced elsewhere.\n\nHere are some suggestions to address the possible issue:\n\n1. **Execution Environment:**\n   Ensure that the script is being executed as a standalone module. If the function is meant to be defined in the same file and called within it, ensure that the function definitions are not encapsulated in unnecessary conditional blocks or nested scopes.\n\n2. **File Separation:**\n   Verify that your code is all in one file as expected, and `rotate_mp3_files` is indeed defined where you think it is. If you have multiple files or imports, make sure that the function is imported properly where `main()` is being executed.\n\n3. **Code Consistency:**\n   Sometimes, copying and pasting code snippets can lead to overlooked discrepancies. Double-check that all your definitions and function calls are consistent and correctly indented, 