ed successfully to {output_path}")\n\n# Verify file exists\nif os.path.exists(output_path):\n    file_size = os.path.getsize(output_path)\n    print(f"  - File size: {file_size:,} bytes")\nelse:\n    print(f"\u2717 ERROR: File {output_path} was not created!")\n```\n\n5. For plot/figure files:\n```python\nimport os\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n# Ensure directory exists\noutput_path = \'{filepath}\'\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_path), exist_ok=True)\n\n# Save plot\nplt.savefig(output_path, dpi=300, bbox_inches=\'tight\')\nprint(f"\u2713 Plot saved successfully to {output_path}")\n\n# Verify file exists\nif os.path.exists(output_path):\n    file_size = os.path.getsize(output_path)\n    print(f"  - File size: {file_size:,} bytes")\nelse:\n    print(f"\u2717 ERROR: File {output_path} was not created!")\n\nplt.close()  # Important: close the figure to free memory\n```\n\n\nCOMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID:\n\u274c Only creating data without saving it\n\u274c Using print() instead of file operations\n\u274c Forgetting to create directories\n\u274c Not verifying file creation\n\u274c Using wrong file paths\n\nCORRECT APPROACH:\n\u2713 Process/create data\n\u2713 Ensure directory exists\n\u2713 Save data to the specified file path\n\u2713 Verify file was created\n\u2713 Print success message with file info\n\nRemember: If the task says "save to ./temp/data.csv", your code MUST create that exact file!\n\n\nRequirements:\n- Write clean, efficient, and well-commented code\n- Follow the task description precisely\n- Include error handling where appropriate\n- Import all necessary libraries at the beginning\n- Test your code logic mentally before finalizing\n- If creating visualizations, make them clear and informative\n\n\n\U0001f3af FINAL REMINDER: This task requires FILE OUTPUT. Your code MUST include:\n1. The actual file writing operation (not just print statements)\n2. Directory creation if needed\n3. File existence verification\n4. Success confirmation message\n\nDoub