ary task is to aid in training a ResNet18 model to predict image rotation angles (a form of self-supervised learning) and potentially use this for classification tasks on the CIFAR-10 dataset.\n\n### Functions and Classes\n\n1. **rotate_img(img, rot)**\n   - **Purpose**: Rotate an image by the specified angle.\n   - **Incomplete Segment**: The implementation for rotations of 90, 180, and 270 degrees is missing. This needs to be implemented possibly using image transformation methods provided by libraries like PIL in conjunction with `torchvision.transforms`.\n\n2. **CIFAR10Rotation(torchvision.datasets.CIFAR10)**\n   - **Purpose**: Inherits from the `torchvision.datasets.CIFAR10` and augments it with the ability to add random rotations while fetching items.\n   - **Methods**: \n     - `__len__()`: Returns the dataset length.\n     - `__getitem__(index)`: Fetches and rotates an image randomly. Returns the original image, rotated image, rotation label, and class label.\n\n3. **imshow(img)**\n   - **Purpose**: Display images in their true color form after unnormalizing.\n   - **Comments**: Utilizes Matplotlib to visually inspect image batches.\n\n4. **run_test(net, testloader, criterion, task)**\n   - **Purpose**: Evaluate the network\'s performance on a test set.\n   - **Incomplete Segment**: The section to calculate the network\'s outputs is missing. One needs to pass images through the network to obtain predictions.\n\n5. **adjust_learning_rate(optimizer, epoch, init_lr, decay_epochs=30)**\n   - **Purpose**: Adjusts the learning rate dynamically based on the epoch, reducing it every `decay_epochs` to allow for finer learning over time.\n\n### Key Variables and Operations\n- **Transformations**: \n  - `transform_train` and `transform_test` define pre-processing steps that include normalization and random augmentations for training (cropping, flipping).\n  \n- **Data Loaders**: \n  - Use `CIFAR10Rotation` to create `trainloader` and `testloader` for loading batches of